DEBUG Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c5441bc6-c1ba-4c35-b8c0-643980cdeb65', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': '', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': '\nYou are a data science expert tasked with selecting and ranking the most appropriate ML libraries for a specific task.\n\n### Task Description:\n**Task Type:** Image classification (binary classification)\n\n**Input Format:**  \n- Input images of skin lesions (image files; image file names are referenced in the dataset as `image_name`).\n- For prediction, a folder path containing new images.\n\n**Prediction Output Format:**  \n- For each input image, output a malignancy probability (a float between 0 and 1).\n\n**Additional Details:**  \n- The model should classify each lesion as malignant or benign.\n- The evaluation metric is Area Under the Receiver Operator Curve (AUROC).\n- The trained model should be saved.\n- A function must be provided that takes a folder path of new images and returns a malignancy probability for each image.\n\n### Data Information:\nAbsolute path to the folder: /home/anri21/be-fair/mlzero/addition_1_data\n\nFiles structures:\n\n----------\n\nAbsolute path: /home/anri21/be-fair/mlzero/addition_1_data/descriptions.txt\nContent:\nText preview:\nI\'m a dermatologist. My colleagues and I have curated a skin lesion dataset over the past several years. I need a model trained on this data to classify lesions as malignant or benign. The trained model should be saved, and I need a function that takes a folder path of new images and returns a malignancy probability (0–1) for each image. Be fair towards skin tone.\nEvaluation metric: Area under the receiver operator curve (AUROC)\n\n----------\nAbsolute path: /home/anri21/be-fair/mlzero/addition_1_data/mydataset.csv\nContent:\nColumns: [\'Unnamed: 0\', \'super_label\', \'skin_tone\', \'alternative_skin_tone\', \'expert_opinion\', \'label\', \'image_name\']\n Unnamed: 0        super_label  skin_tone  alternative_skin_tone expert_opinion          label image_name\n          0       inflammatory          2                      2            NaN non-neoplastic    image_1\n          1       inflammatory          4                      5            NaN non-neoplastic    image_2\n          2 malignant melanoma          2                      1            NaN      malignant    image_3\n\n----------\n\n\n### Available ML Libraries:\nLibrary Name: FlagEmbedding\nVersion: v1.3.4\nDescription: FlagEmbedding specializes in retrieval and reranking tasks.\n\n\nLibrary Name: machine learning\nVersion: v0.1.0\nDescription: You should select this as a general reference of machine learning or deep learning algorithms in case other tools are not helpful.\n\n\nLibrary Name: wav2vec2\nVersion: v0.0.0\nDescription: This model was pre-trained on 4.5M hours of unlabeled audio data covering more than 143 languages. It requires finetuning to be used for downstream tasks such as Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR), or Audio Classification.\n\n\nLibrary Name: qwen3\nVersion: v0.0.0\nDescription: Qwen3-0.6B is a compact 0.6 billion parameter text generation model that uniquely switches between thinking and non-thinking modes for both efficient dialogue and complex reasoning tasks.\n\n\nLibrary Name: autogluon.tabular\nVersion: v1.4.0.dev\nDescription: AutoGluon Tabular automates ML model training for tabular data, excelling at numerical and categorical data processing. It doesn\'t support NLP or image-based tasks.\n\n\nLibrary Name: autogluon.multimodal\nVersion: v1.4.0.dev\nDescription: AutoGluon Multimodal excels at multimodal classification, regression, document classification, and semantic segmentation tasks. The framework is not optimized for pure tabular data processing and DOES NOT support generative tasks (image generation, text generation, etc.) or audio-related tasks. It also doesn\'t handle object detection.\n\n\nLibrary Name: autogluon.timeseries\nVersion: v1.4.0.dev\nDescription: AutoGluon TimeSeries automates forecasting model training for time series data, supporting both univariate and multivariate predictions.\n\n\n\n\nIMPORTANT: Your response MUST follow this exact format:\n---\nEXPLANATION: <provide your detailed reasoning process for evaluating the libraries>\n\nRANKED_LIBRARIES:\n1. <first choice library name>\n2. <second choice library name>\n3. <third choice library name>\n...\n---\n\nRequirements for your response:\n1. First provide a detailed explanation of your reasoning process using the "EXPLANATION:" header\n2. Then provide a ranking of libraries using the "RANKED_LIBRARIES:" header\n3. The library names must be exactly as shown in the available libraries list\n4. Provide a ranking of at least 3 libraries (if available)\n5. In your explanation, analyze each library\'s strengths and weaknesses for this specific task\n6. Consider the task requirements, data characteristics, and library features\n\nDo not include any other formatting or additional sections in your response.\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1', 'max_completion_tokens': 32768, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
